From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rmem: validate direction and range of RMEN_CMD_FLUSH_CACHE

On top of 0001-0099.

The /dev/rmem flush ioctl handed the user's {addr, len, dir} straight to
dma_cache_sync():

 - dir 3 (DMA_NONE) hits BUG_ON() in dma_cache_sync(), any dir >= 4 hits
   BUG() in __dma_sync_virtual(); one ioctl from any process that can
   open /dev/rmem took the kernel down.  Now -EINVAL.
 - addr/len were not checked: a kernel address, a hole, a PROT_NONE
   mapping or a range running past the end of a mapping made the cache
   instructions fault in kernel mode without a fixup (oops).  The range
   must now start in an accessible mapping of the caller; it is clamped
   to the accessible mappings that follow contiguously (a flush rounded
   up past the end of a buffer keeps the part that matters), otherwise
   -EFAULT.  len 0 is a no-op; an overflowing or above-TASK_SIZE range is
   -EFAULT.

Valid callers (libimp/OpenIMP: rmem VA, dir 1/2, inside the arena) see no
change.  This is the 3.10 driver, which flushes by virtual address; the
4.4 T41 driver takes a physical address and is not touched here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/misc/rmem.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/rmem.c
@@ -46,14 +46,49 @@
 static long rmem_cmd_flush_cache(long arg)
 {
 	struct rmem_flush_cache_info info;
-	long ret = 0;
+	struct mm_struct *mm = current->mm;
+	struct vm_area_struct *vma;
+	unsigned long addr, end;
+
 	if (copy_from_user(&info, (void *)arg, sizeof(info))) {
 		return -EFAULT;
 	}
 
+	/* dma_cache_sync() hits BUG_ON() for DMA_NONE (3) and BUG() for any
+	 * other unknown direction. */
+	if (!valid_dma_direction(info.dir))
+		return -EINVAL;
+	if (!info.len)
+		return 0;
+
+	addr = info.addr;
+	end = addr + info.len;
+	if (end < addr || end > TASK_SIZE || !mm)
+		return -EFAULT;
+
+	/* The cache instructions run on the caller's virtual address. A hole,
+	 * a PROT_NONE mapping or a kernel address faults in kernel mode without
+	 * a fixup and oopses, so flush only the accessible mappings that run
+	 * contiguously from the start address and refuse a start that is not
+	 * mapped. mmap_sem is dropped before the cache operation because a
+	 * page fault there takes it again. */
+	down_read(&mm->mmap_sem);
+	while (addr < end) {
+		vma = find_vma(mm, addr);
+		if (!vma || vma->vm_start > addr ||
+		    !(vma->vm_flags & (VM_READ | VM_WRITE)))
+			break;
+		addr = vma->vm_end;
+	}
+	up_read(&mm->mmap_sem);
+	if (addr == info.addr)
+		return -EFAULT;
+	if (addr < end)
+		info.len = addr - info.addr;
+
 	dma_cache_sync(NULL, (void *)info.addr, info.len, info.dir);
 
-	return ret;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static long rmem_ioctl(struct file *filp, unsigned int cmd, unsigned long arg)
